5. Entity Resolution should be conservative


This is one of the most important pieces.


Don't let an embedding model directly merge entities.


Instead:


candidate generation → similarity → contextual validation → temporal validation → graph validation → confidence → merge/reject


And maintain:


ENTITY_A
   │
   ├── POSSIBLE_MATCH → ENTITY_B
   │
   ├── CONFIRMED_MATCH → ENTITY_C
   │
   └── HISTORICAL_IDENTITY → ENTITY_D



That lets NEXUS represent uncertainty rather than destroying information through an incorrect merge.


6. The Query Engine becomes the heart of NEXUS


The frontend shouldn't ask:




“Give me everything around this coordinate.”




It should ask:




“Project the best-supported world state satisfying this QueryContext.”




For example:


QueryContext
├── spatial_extent
├── temporal_extent
├── entity_types
├── relationship_constraints
├── confidence_threshold
├── evidence_requirements
├── resolution
├── freshness_requirement
└── epistemic_policy



The projection engine then produces:


WORLD STATE
      ↓
FILTER
      ↓
TEMPORAL RECONSTRUCTION
      ↓
EVIDENCE/CONFIDENCE EVALUATION
      ↓
SPATIAL AGGREGATION
      ↓
LOD SELECTION
      ↓
VECTOR/TENSOR REPRESENTATION
      ↓
WebGPU



7. WebGPU should be a projection system, not the database


Your WebGPU idea is excellent, but I would keep the rendering architecture completely decoupled from storage.


The browser receives renderable state, not raw database records.


For example:


World State
   ↓
Projection Engine
   ↓
GPU-ready binary tiles
   ↓
WebGPU
   ↓
visual representation



That makes it possible to replace the visualization layer without redesigning the world model.


8. ZK provenance should be selective


Don't generate expensive zk-SNARKs for every assertion by default.


Use tiers:


LEVEL 0
hash integrity

LEVEL 1
digital signature

LEVEL 2
Merkle inclusion proof

LEVEL 3
reproducible transformation proof

LEVEL 4
zero-knowledge computation proof

LEVEL 5
externally anchored state commitment



High-value/high-risk assertions can receive stronger verification.


9. Conflict resolution should NOT automatically choose “truth”


Instead:


ASSERTION A ─────┐
                 ├── CONFLICT SET
ASSERTION B ─────┤
                 │
ASSERTION C ─────┘
                      ↓
              Evidence Evaluation
                      ↓
             ┌────────┼────────┐
             ↓        ↓        ↓
          A favored  B favored  unresolved



NEXUS should be capable of returning:




UNKNOWN




That is a feature, not a failure.


